/-!
# Divided power polynomial algebras

For a divided power ring `(A, I, γ)` and a finite family of variables, the divided power
polynomial algebra has a canonical divided power structure on the sum of the extension of `I`
and the augmentation ideal. Its divided powers on a variable are the corresponding divided
power monomials, and it is free on elements of a target divided power ideal.

## Main definitions

* `DividedPowers.dividedPowerPolynomialMonomialBasis` identifies Mathlib's divided power algebra
  with the free module on divided power monomials.
* `DividedPowers.dividedPowerPolynomialPositiveIdeal` is the augmentation ideal.
* `DividedPowers.dividedPowerPolynomialIdeal` is the sum of the extended coefficient ideal and
  the augmentation ideal.
* `DividedPowers.dividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowers` is the canonical divided power structure on
  this ideal.
* `DividedPowers.dividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowerRing` bundles the resulting divided power
  ring.

## Main results

* `DividedPowers.monomial_span_eq_top` and `DividedPowers.monomial_linearIndependent` say that
  the divided power monomials form a basis of the algebra over the coefficient ring.
* `DividedPowers.positiveIdeal_eq_span_monomials` says that the augmentation ideal is generated
  by the divided power monomials with nonzero exponent vector, and
  `DividedPowers.positiveIdeal_eq_span_variableMonomials` that it is already generated by the
  one-variable divided powers `xᵢ^[m]` with `m ≠ 0`.
* `DividedPowers.coefficient_injective` and `DividedPowers.coefficient_flat` say that the
  coefficient map is injective and flat.
* `DividedPowers.dividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowers_dpow_variable` computes the divided powers
  of the variables.
* `DividedPowers.dividedPowerPolynomialCoefficient_isDPMorphism` says that the coefficient map is
  a morphism of divided power rings.
* `DividedPowers.dividedPowerPolynomialDividedPowers_unique` gives uniqueness of the structure.
* `DividedPowers.existsUnique_dPMorphism_from_dividedPowerPolynomial` is the universal property.

## Implementation notes

The algebra `A⟨xᵢ : i ∈ ι⟩` is represented by
`DividedPowerAlgebra A (ι →₀ A)`. The basis
`dividedPowerPolynomialMonomialBasis` identifies this quotient presentation with the source's
direct sum `⊕ (n : ι →₀ ℕ), A · ∏ i, xᵢ^[n i]`. Taking an arbitrary universe-polymorphic finite
type `ι` both specializes to `Fin t` and permits finite subsets of an arbitrary index type to be
used without reindexing.

The divided power structure itself is not built by hand on `A⟨xᵢ : i ∈ ι⟩`. It is obtained from
the integral model `DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ)`, where the generator criterion applies
because the algebra is free over `ℤ` on the divided power monomials, hence torsion free. That
structure is transported in two steps: first by flat base change along
`ℤ → ℤ[xₐ : a ∈ A]`, which is free and therefore flat, and then along the surjection
`ℤ[xₐ : a ∈ A] → A` of a polynomial presentation of the coefficient ring, whose kernel meets the
augmentation ideal in a product of ideals and is consequently a sub-divided-power ideal. The
private machinery of this file — the integral monomial basis, the tensor identification
`A ⊗_ℤ ℤ⟨xᵢ⟩ ≃ A⟨xᵢ⟩` and the polynomial presentation of `A` — exists to carry out exactly
this transport.

The universal property is stated as a unique lifting property. Thus its uniqueness makes the
lifting canonical and records the correspondence in the source without making an arbitrary
choice of inverse maps.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07H5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07H5)
-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

namespace DividedPowers

universe u v w

/-- The divided power monomial `∏ i, xᵢ^[n i]`. -/
public def dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial (A : Type u) [CommSemiring A] {ι : Type w}
    (n : ι →₀ ℕ) : DividedPowerAlgebra A (ι →₀ A) :=
  n.prod fun i m ↦ DividedPowerAlgebra.dp A m (Finsupp.single i 1)

/-- The divided power monomials span the divided power polynomial algebra as a module over the
coefficient ring. -/
public theorem monomial_span_eq_top (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (ι : Type w) :
    Submodule.span A (Set.range (dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial A (ι := ι))) = ⊤ := by
  apply DividedPowerAlgebra.submodule_span_prod_dp_eq_top
  simpa only [show (fun i : ι ↦ Finsupp.single i (1 : A)) =
      (Finsupp.basisSingleOne : Module.Basis ι A (ι →₀ A)) from rfl] using
    (Finsupp.basisSingleOne : Module.Basis ι A (ι →₀ A)).span_eq

private theorem factorial_dvd_multinomial_nsmul_singleton
    (n m : ℕ) (hm : m ≠ 0) :
    n.factorial ∣ (n • ({m} : Multiset ℕ)).multinomial := by
  have hspec : m.factorial ^ n * (n • ({m} : Multiset ℕ)).multinomial =
      (n * m).factorial := by
    rw [Multiset.multinomial_nsmul_singleton]
    simpa [Finset.prod_const, Finset.sum_const_zero, nsmul_eq_mul] using
      (Nat.multinomial_spec (Finset.range n) (fun _ ↦ m))
  have hu : (n * m).factorial =
      m.factorial ^ n * (n.uniformBell m * n.factorial) := by
    rw [← Nat.uniformBell_mul_eq n hm]
    ring
  have heq : (n • ({m} : Multiset ℕ)).multinomial =
      n.uniformBell m * n.factorial :=
    Nat.eq_of_mul_eq_mul_left (by positivity) (hspec.trans hu)
  exact ⟨n.uniformBell m, by rw [heq, mul_comm]⟩

private noncomputable def rationalMonomialEvaluation (ι : Type w) :
    DividedPowerAlgebra ℚ (ι →₀ ℚ) →ₐ[ℚ] MvPolynomial ι ℚ := by
  classical
  exact DividedPowerAlgebra.lift
    (_root_.DividedPowers.RatAlgebra.dividedPowers (⊤ : Ideal (MvPolynomial ι ℚ)))
    (Finsupp.linearCombination ℚ (MvPolynomial.X : ι → MvPolynomial ι ℚ))
    (fun _ ↦ Submodule.mem_top)

private theorem rationalMonomialEvaluation_dp (ι : Type w) (i : ι) (n : ℕ) :
    rationalMonomialEvaluation ι (DividedPowerAlgebra.dp ℚ n (Finsupp.single i 1)) =
      Ring.inverse (n.factorial : MvPolynomial ι ℚ) *
        (MvPolynomial.X i : MvPolynomial ι ℚ) ^ n := by
  classical
  unfold rationalMonomialEvaluation
  rw [DividedPowerAlgebra.lift_apply_dp]
  simp only [Finsupp.linearCombination_single, one_smul]
  simp [_root_.DividedPowers.RatAlgebra.dpow_apply]

private theorem inverse_factorial_moore (ι : Type w) (m : ℕ) :
    Ring.inverse (m.factorial : MvPolynomial ι ℚ) =
      MvPolynomial.C ((m.factorial : ℚ)⁻¹) := by
  have hu : IsUnit (m.factorial : MvPolynomial ι ℚ) :=
    IsUnit.natCast_factorial_of_algebra ℚ m
  rw [← mul_one (Ring.inverse (m.factorial : MvPolynomial ι ℚ))]
  apply (Ring.inverse_mul_eq_iff_eq_mul _ 1 _ hu).2
  have hf : (m.factorial : ℚ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast Nat.factorial_ne_zero m
  show (1 : MvPolynomial ι ℚ) =
    MvPolynomial.C (m.factorial : ℚ) * MvPolynomial.C ((m.factorial : ℚ)⁻¹)
  rw [← map_mul, mul_inv_cancel₀ hf, map_one]

private theorem rationalMonomialEvaluation_monomial (ι : Type w) (n : ι →₀ ℕ) :
    rationalMonomialEvaluation ι (dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial ℚ n) =
      n.prod (fun i m ↦ Ring.inverse (m.factorial : MvPolynomial ι ℚ) *
        (MvPolynomial.X i : MvPolynomial ι ℚ) ^ m) := by
  simp only [dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial, map_finsuppProd]
  exact Finsupp.prod_congr (fun i _ ↦ rationalMonomialEvaluation_dp ι i (n i))

private theorem rationalMonomialEvaluation_monomial_eq_smul (ι : Type w) (n : ι →₀ ℕ) :
    rationalMonomialEvaluation ι (dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial ℚ n) =
      (n.prod fun _ m ↦ (m.factorial : ℚ)⁻¹) •
        MvPolynomial.monomial n (1 : ℚ) := by
  rw [rationalMonomialEvaluation_monomial]
  simp_rw [inverse_factorial_moore]
  rw [Finsupp.prod_mul, ← map_finsuppProd, ← MvPolynomial.monic_monomial_eq]
  simp [Algebra.smul_def]

private theorem rational_monomial_linearIndependent (ι : Type w) :
    LinearIndependent ℚ (dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial ℚ (ι := ι)) := by
  classical
  let q : (ι →₀ ℕ) → ℚ := fun n ↦ n.prod fun _ m ↦ (m.factorial : ℚ)⁻¹
  have hq (n : ι →₀ ℕ) : q n ≠ 0 :=
    Finsupp.prod_ne_zero_iff.mpr fun i _ ↦
      inv_ne_zero (by exact_mod_cast Nat.factorial_ne_zero (n i))
  let w : (ι →₀ ℕ) → ℚˣ := fun n ↦ Units.mk0 (q n) (hq n)
  have hmono : LinearIndependent ℚ (fun n : ι →₀ ℕ ↦
      MvPolynomial.monomial n (1 : ℚ)) := by
    simpa only [MvPolynomial.coe_basisMonomials] using
      (MvPolynomial.basisMonomials ι ℚ).linearIndependent
  have hscaled := hmono.units_smul w
  have heq : (fun n : ι →₀ ℕ ↦
      rationalMonomialEvaluation ι (dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial ℚ n)) =
        w • (fun n : ι →₀ ℕ ↦ MvPolynomial.monomial n (1 : ℚ)) :=
    funext (rationalMonomialEvaluation_monomial_eq_smul ι)
  rw [← heq] at hscaled
  exact LinearIndependent.of_comp (rationalMonomialEvaluation ι).toLinearMap hscaled

private noncomputable def integralToCoefficientDividedPowerAlgebra
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (ι : Type w) :
    DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ) →ₐ[ℤ]
      DividedPowerAlgebra A (ι →₀ A) :=
  DividedPowerAlgebra.map A
    (Finsupp.mapRange.linearMap (Algebra.linearMap ℤ A))

private theorem integralToCoefficientDividedPowerAlgebra_monomial
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (ι : Type w) (n : ι →₀ ℕ) :
    integralToCoefficientDividedPowerAlgebra A ι
        (dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial ℤ n) =
      dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial A n := by
  classical
  simp only [dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial, map_finsuppProd]
  apply Finsupp.prod_congr
  intro i hi
  simp [integralToCoefficientDividedPowerAlgebra,
    DividedPowerAlgebra.map_apply_dp]

private theorem integral_monomial_linearIndependent (ι : Type w) :
    LinearIndependent ℤ (dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial ℤ (ι := ι)) := by
  have hq : LinearIndependent ℤ (dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial ℚ (ι := ι)) :=
    (rational_monomial_linearIndependent ι).restrict_scalars' ℤ
  have hmap : LinearIndependent ℤ (fun n : ι →₀ ℕ ↦
      integralToCoefficientDividedPowerAlgebra ℚ ι (dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial ℤ n)) := by
    simpa only [integralToCoefficientDividedPowerAlgebra_monomial ℚ] using hq
  exact LinearIndependent.of_comp
    (integralToCoefficientDividedPowerAlgebra ℚ ι).toLinearMap hmap

private noncomputable def integralMonomialBasis (ι : Type w) :
    Module.Basis (ι →₀ ℕ) ℤ (DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ)) :=
  Module.Basis.mk (integral_monomial_linearIndependent ι)
    (by rw [monomial_span_eq_top])

private theorem integralMonomialBasis_apply (ι : Type w) (n : ι →₀ ℕ) :
    integralMonomialBasis ι n = dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial ℤ n := by
  unfold integralMonomialBasis
  exact Module.Basis.mk_apply _ _ n

private noncomputable def scalarExtensionToCoefficientDividedPowerAlgebra
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (ι : Type w) :
    TensorProduct ℤ A (DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ)) →ₐ[A]
      DividedPowerAlgebra A (ι →₀ A) :=
  (Algebra.TensorProduct.liftEquivRight ℤ A
    (DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ))
    (DividedPowerAlgebra A (ι →₀ A)))
      (integralToCoefficientDividedPowerAlgebra A ι)

private theorem scalarExtensionToCoefficientDividedPowerAlgebra_tmul
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (ι : Type w) (a : A)
    (b : DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ)) :
    scalarExtensionToCoefficientDividedPowerAlgebra A ι
        (TensorProduct.tmul ℤ a b) =
      algebraMap A (DividedPowerAlgebra A (ι →₀ A)) a *
        integralToCoefficientDividedPowerAlgebra A ι b := by
  simp [scalarExtensionToCoefficientDividedPowerAlgebra,
    Algebra.TensorProduct.liftEquivRight_apply, Algebra.TensorProduct.lift_tmul]

private theorem integral_dividedPowerAlgebra_hasUniqueDiv (ι : Type w) :
    HasUniqueDiv (DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ)) := by
  let : Module.Free ℤ (DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ)) :=
    Module.Free.of_basis (integralMonomialBasis ι)
  exact (Module.isTorsionFree_int_iff_hasUniqueDiv
    (M := DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ))).mp inferInstance

private theorem integral_dividedPowerAlgebra_isAddTorsionFree (ι : Type w) :
    IsAddTorsionFree (DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ)) :=
  have := integral_dividedPowerAlgebra_hasUniqueDiv ι
  inferInstance

private def coefficientPresentation (A : Type u) [CommRing A] :
    MvPolynomial A ℤ →+* A :=
  (MvPolynomial.aeval (fun a : A ↦ a)).toRingHom

private theorem coefficientPresentation_surjective (A : Type u) [CommRing A] :
    Function.Surjective (coefficientPresentation A) := by
  intro a
  refine ⟨MvPolynomial.X a, ?_⟩
  simp [coefficientPresentation]

attribute [local instance 2000] Algebra.toModule in
private theorem integralTensorCoefficientPresentation_surjective
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (ι : Type w) :
    Function.Surjective (Algebra.TensorProduct.map
      (AlgHom.id ℤ (DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ)))
      (MvPolynomial.aeval (fun a : A ↦ a) : MvPolynomial A ℤ →ₐ[ℤ] A)) := by
  apply Algebra.TensorProduct.map_surjective
  · exact Function.surjective_id
  · exact coefficientPresentation_surjective A

attribute [local instance 2000] Algebra.toModule in
private theorem integralTensorCoefficientPresentation_ker
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (ι : Type w) :
    RingHom.ker (Algebra.TensorProduct.map
      (AlgHom.id ℤ (DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ)))
      (MvPolynomial.aeval (fun a : A ↦ a) : MvPolynomial A ℤ →ₐ[ℤ] A)) =
    (RingHom.ker (coefficientPresentation A)).map
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight :
        MvPolynomial A ℤ →ₐ[ℤ]
          TensorProduct ℤ (DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ)) (MvPolynomial A ℤ)) :=
  Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor_ker
    (MvPolynomial.aeval (fun a : A ↦ a) : MvPolynomial A ℤ →ₐ[ℤ] A)
    (coefficientPresentation_surjective A)

private theorem coefficientPresentationRing_flat (A : Type u) [CommRing A] :
    (algebraMap ℤ (MvPolynomial A ℤ)).Flat := by
  let : Module.Free ℤ (MvPolynomial A ℤ) :=
    Module.Free.of_basis (MvPolynomial.basisMonomials A ℤ)
  exact RingHom.flat_algebraMap_iff.mpr inferInstance

/-- The augmentation `A⟨xᵢ : i ∈ ι⟩ →ₐ[A] A`, sending every variable to zero. -/
public def dividedPowerPolynomialAugmentation (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (ι : Type w) :
    DividedPowerAlgebra A (ι →₀ A) →ₐ[A] A :=
  DividedPowerAlgebra.lift (dividedPowersBot A) 0 (fun _ ↦ by simp)

/-- The coefficient map `A → A⟨xᵢ : i ∈ ι⟩` is injective: the augmentation is a retraction of
it. -/
public theorem coefficient_injective (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (ι : Type w) :
    Function.Injective (algebraMap A (DividedPowerAlgebra A (ι →₀ A))) := by
  intro a b h
  have := congrArg (dividedPowerPolynomialAugmentation A ι) h
  simpa using this

private theorem integralAugmentation_surjective (ι : Type w) :
    Function.Surjective (dividedPowerPolynomialAugmentation ℤ ι) := by
  intro z
  refine ⟨algebraMap ℤ (DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ)) z, ?_⟩
  exact (dividedPowerPolynomialAugmentation ℤ ι).commutes z

/-- The positive-degree ideal `A⟨xᵢ : i ∈ ι⟩₊`, defined as the augmentation ideal. -/
public def dividedPowerPolynomialPositiveIdeal (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (ι : Type w) :
    Ideal (DividedPowerAlgebra A (ι →₀ A)) :=
  RingHom.ker (dividedPowerPolynomialAugmentation A ι).toRingHom

/-- The ideal `I A⟨xᵢ : i ∈ ι⟩ + A⟨xᵢ : i ∈ ι⟩₊`. -/
public def dividedPowerPolynomialIdeal {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A)
    (ι : Type w) : Ideal (DividedPowerAlgebra A (ι →₀ A)) :=
  Ideal.map (algebraMap A (DividedPowerAlgebra A (ι →₀ A))) I +
    dividedPowerPolynomialPositiveIdeal A ι

/-- The variable `xᵢ` in the divided power polynomial algebra. -/
public def dividedPowerPolynomialVariable (A : Type u) [CommSemiring A] {ι : Type w}
    (i : ι) : DividedPowerAlgebra A (ι →₀ A) :=
  DividedPowerAlgebra.dp A 1 (Finsupp.single i 1)

/-- The distinguished divided power monomial `xᵢ^[n]`. -/
public def dividedPowerPolynomialVariableMonomial (A : Type u) [CommSemiring A]
    {ι : Type w} (i : ι) (n : ℕ) : DividedPowerAlgebra A (ι →₀ A) :=
  DividedPowerAlgebra.dp A n (Finsupp.single i 1)

/-- A variable lies in the augmentation ideal. -/
public theorem variable_mem_positiveIdeal (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    {ι : Type w} (i : ι) :
    dividedPowerPolynomialVariable A i ∈ dividedPowerPolynomialPositiveIdeal A ι := by
  classical
  show dividedPowerPolynomialAugmentation A ι
    (DividedPowerAlgebra.dp A 1 (Finsupp.single i 1)) = 0
  simp [dividedPowerPolynomialAugmentation, dividedPowersBot_dpow_eq]

/-- A variable lies in the divided power ideal of the divided power polynomial algebra. -/
public theorem variable_mem_polynomialIdeal (A : DividedPowerRing.{u})
    {ι : Type w} (i : ι) :
    dividedPowerPolynomialVariable A i ∈ dividedPowerPolynomialIdeal A.ideal ι :=
  Ideal.mem_sup_right (variable_mem_positiveIdeal A i)

/-- The image of an element of the coefficient divided power ideal lies in the divided power
ideal of the divided power polynomial algebra. -/
public theorem coefficient_mem_polynomialIdeal (A : DividedPowerRing.{u})
    {ι : Type w} {a : A} (ha : a ∈ A.ideal) :
    algebraMap A (DividedPowerAlgebra A (ι →₀ A)) a ∈
      dividedPowerPolynomialIdeal A.ideal ι :=
  Ideal.mem_sup_left (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha)

/-- A divided power `xᵢ^[n]` with `n ≠ 0` lies in the augmentation ideal. -/
public theorem variableMonomial_mem_positiveIdeal (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    {ι : Type w} (i : ι) {n : ℕ} (hn : n ≠ 0) :
    dividedPowerPolynomialVariableMonomial A i n ∈
      dividedPowerPolynomialPositiveIdeal A ι := by
  classical
  show dividedPowerPolynomialAugmentation A ι
    (DividedPowerAlgebra.dp A n (Finsupp.single i 1)) = 0
  simp [dividedPowerPolynomialAugmentation, dividedPowersBot_dpow_eq, hn]

/-- The augmentation sends a divided power monomial to `1` if its exponent vector is zero and to
`0` otherwise. -/
public theorem augmentation_monomial (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    {ι : Type w} [DecidableEq ι] (n : ι →₀ ℕ) :
    dividedPowerPolynomialAugmentation A ι (dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial A n) =
      if n = 0 then 1 else 0 := by
  classical
  by_cases hn : n = 0
  · subst n
    simp [dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial]
  · rw [ite_eq_right hn]
    have hs : n.support.Nonempty := Finsupp.support_nonempty_iff.mpr hn
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hs
    simp only [dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial, map_finsuppProd]
    exact Finset.prod_eq_zero hi
      (variableMonomial_mem_positiveIdeal A i (Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mp hi))

/-- The augmentation ideal is generated by the divided power monomials with nonzero exponent
vector. -/
public theorem positiveIdeal_eq_span_monomials (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (ι : Type w) :
    dividedPowerPolynomialPositiveIdeal A ι =
      Ideal.span {x | ∃ (n : ι →₀ ℕ), n ≠ 0 ∧ x = dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial A n} := by
  classical
  let P : Ideal (DividedPowerAlgebra A (ι →₀ A)) :=
    Ideal.span {x | ∃ (n : ι →₀ ℕ), n ≠ 0 ∧ x = dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial A n}
  have hgen : ∀ x : DividedPowerAlgebra A (ι →₀ A),
      x - algebraMap A _ (dividedPowerPolynomialAugmentation A ι x) ∈ P := by
    intro x
    have hx : x ∈ Submodule.span A
        (Set.range (dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial A (ι := ι))) := by
      rw [monomial_span_eq_top]
      trivial
    induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem x hx =>
      obtain ⟨n, rfl⟩ := hx
      by_cases hn : n = 0
      · subst n
        simp [dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial]
      · rw [augmentation_monomial A n, ite_eq_right hn, map_zero, sub_zero]
        exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨n, hn, rfl⟩
    | zero => simp
    | add x y _ _ hx hy =>
      simpa only [map_add, sub_add_sub_comm] using P.add_mem hx hy
    | smul a x _ hx =>
      simpa [Algebra.smul_def, map_mul, mul_sub] using
        Submodule.smul_of_tower_mem P a hx
  show RingHom.ker (dividedPowerPolynomialAugmentation A ι).toRingHom = P
  apply le_antisymm
  · intro x hx
    have hax : dividedPowerPolynomialAugmentation A ι x = 0 := hx
    simpa [hax] using hgen x
  · apply Ideal.span_le.mpr
    rintro x ⟨n, hn, rfl⟩
    show dividedPowerPolynomialAugmentation A ι
      (dividedPowerPolynomialMonomial A n) = 0
    simp [augmentation_monomial A n, hn]

/-- The augmentation ideal is generated by the one-variable divided powers `xᵢ^[m]` with
`m ≠ 0`. -/
public theorem positiveIdeal_eq_span_variableMonomials (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (ι : Type w) :
    dividedPowerPolynomialPositiveIdeal A ι =
      Ideal.span {x | ∃ (i : ι) (m : ℕ), m ≠ 0 ∧
        x = dividedPowerPolynomialVariableMonomial A i m} := by
  classical
  rw [positiveIdeal_eq_span_monomials]
  apply le_antisymm
  · refine Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_
    rintro x ⟨n, hn, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := Finsupp.support_nonempty_iff.mpr hn
    have hni : n i ≠ 0 := Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mp hi
    show n.prod (fun i m ↦ DividedPowerAlgebra.dp A m (Finsupp.single i 1)) ∈ _
    rw [← n.mul_prod_erase' i
      (fun j m ↦ DividedPowerAlgebra.dp A m (Finsupp.single j 1))
      (fun j ↦ DividedPowerAlgebra.dp_zero (m := Finsupp.single j (1 : A)))]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, n i, hni, rfl⟩)
  · apply Ideal.span_le.mpr
    rintro x ⟨i, m, hm, rfl⟩
    have hx := variableMonomial_mem_positiveIdeal A i hm
    rw [positiveIdeal_eq_span_monomials] at hx
    exact hx

/-- The ideal `I A⟨xᵢ⟩ + A⟨xᵢ⟩₊` lies in any ideal containing the image of `I` and the
divided powers `xᵢ^[m]` with `m ≠ 0`. -/
private theorem polynomialIdeal_le_of_mem (A : DividedPowerRing.{u}) (ι : Type w)
    (J : Ideal (DividedPowerAlgebra A (ι →₀ A)))
    (hc : ∀ ⦃a : A⦄, a ∈ A.ideal → algebraMap A (DividedPowerAlgebra A (ι →₀ A)) a ∈ J)
    (hv : ∀ (i : ι) (m : ℕ), m ≠ 0 → dividedPowerPolynomialVariableMonomial A i m ∈ J) :
    dividedPowerPolynomialIdeal A.ideal ι ≤ J := by
  refine sup_le (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr hc) ?_
  rw [positiveIdeal_eq_span_variableMonomials, Ideal.span_le]
  rintro x ⟨i, m, hm, rfl⟩
  exact hv i m hm

private noncomputable def integralPositiveDividedPowers (ι : Type w) :
    _root_.DividedPowers (dividedPowerPolynomialPositiveIdeal ℤ ι) := by
  let : HasUniqueDiv (DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ)) :=
    integral_dividedPowerAlgebra_hasUniqueDiv ι
  apply Classical.choice
  rw [nonempty_dividedPowers_iff_exists_generators_pow_mem_factorial_mul]
  refine ⟨{x | ∃ (i : ι) (m : ℕ), m ≠ 0 ∧
      x = dividedPowerPolynomialVariableMonomial ℤ i m},
    (positiveIdeal_eq_span_variableMonomials ℤ ι).symm, ?_⟩
  rintro x ⟨i, m, hm, rfl⟩ n hn
  have hn0 : n ≠ 0 := by omega
  have hmem : dividedPowerPolynomialVariableMonomial ℤ i (n * m) ∈
      dividedPowerPolynomialPositiveIdeal ℤ ι :=
    variableMonomial_mem_positiveIdeal ℤ i (mul_ne_zero hn0 hm)
  have hdvd := factorial_dvd_multinomial_nsmul_singleton n m hm
  have hfac : ((n • ({m} : Multiset ℕ)).multinomial :
      DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ)) ∈
      Ideal.span {(n.factorial : DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ))} := by
    apply Ideal.mem_span_singleton.mpr
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := hdvd
    refine ⟨(k : DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ)), ?_⟩
    simpa only [Nat.cast_mul] using
      congrArg (fun a : ℕ ↦ (a : DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ))) hk
  change (DividedPowerAlgebra.dp ℤ m (Finsupp.single i 1)) ^ n ∈ _
  rw [DividedPowerAlgebra.pow_dp]
  exact Ideal.mul_mem_mul hfac hmem

private theorem integralPositiveDividedPowers_dpow_variable
    (ι : Type w) (i : ι) (n : ℕ) :
    (integralPositiveDividedPowers ι).dpow n
        (dividedPowerPolynomialVariable ℤ i) =
      dividedPowerPolynomialVariableMonomial ℤ i n := by
  let : HasUniqueDiv (DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ)) :=
    integral_dividedPowerAlgebra_hasUniqueDiv ι
  apply nsmul_right_injective (Nat.factorial_ne_zero n)
  have hfac := (integralPositiveDividedPowers ι).factorial_mul_dpow_eq_pow
    (n := n) (variable_mem_positiveIdeal ℤ i)
  have hdp := DividedPowerAlgebra.natFactorial_mul_dp_eq (R := ℤ) n
    (Finsupp.single i (1 : ℤ))
  simpa [dividedPowerPolynomialVariable, dividedPowerPolynomialVariableMonomial,
    nsmul_eq_mul] using hfac.trans hdp.symm

private noncomputable def integralPositiveDividedPowerRing (ι : Type w) :
    DividedPowerRing.{w} :=
  .of (DividedPowerAlgebra ℤ (ι →₀ ℤ))
    (dividedPowerPolynomialPositiveIdeal ℤ ι)
